<section class="band"><div class="wrap"><div class="head"><span class="eyebrow">Before you start</span><h2>First, understand what is open.</h2><p class="lede">This is a personal digital exposure assessment service, not legal advice or an investigation. The first message is short and neutral, with no details, screenshots, or passwords. You decide whether and when to make contact.</p><p class="lede">There is no need to send personal information, documents, or a detailed account in the first message. It is enough to say that you want to understand what may be exposed.</p></div></div></section>

<section class="band"><div class="wrap"><div class="head"><span class="eyebrow">Why timing matters</span><h2>A sudden change can be noticed.</h2><p class="lede">Changing a password, turning off location sharing, or removing a device can be visible to someone connected to an account or following alerts. What to change, and when, depends on your situation. The aim is not to reveal a change before you understand the full picture.</p></div></div></section>

<section class="band"><div class="wrap"><div class="head"><span class="eyebrow">Before you change</span><h2>Sometimes it makes sense to begin with a separate account or device.</h2><p class="lede">Sometimes the first step is a separate starting point: a device or account that was not connected to the other side, rather than immediately changing something they can already reach. In an assessment, we can understand where you are exposed, what makes sense to change, and in what order. Nothing is done remotely, nothing is uploaded to the cloud, and no log of your digital life is kept.</p></div></div></section>

<section class="band"><div class="wrap"><div class="head"><span class="eyebrow">What not to do abruptly</span><h2>Do not close everything at once.</h2><p class="lede">Do not rush to close access to every account, confront another person with what you found, or assume that one change solved the problem. We will not promise that a change will be invisible, or that everything can be finished in one day. First understand. Then decide.</p></div></div></section>

<section class="band"><div class="wrap cred"><div class="cred-lead"><span class="eyebrow">How to reach us</span><h2>A private conversation, at your pace.</h2><p>Reach us through WhatsApp or Signal with a short, neutral message. No passwords, screenshots, or intimate details in the first message. We will clarify the next step and timing, in person and discreetly.</p></div><ul class="cred-list"><li><b>First contact:</b> WhatsApp or Signal only, with a short, neutral message.</li><li><b>Do not send:</b> passwords, screenshots, legal documents, or detailed allegations.</li><li><b>What happens next:</b> we confirm that the service fits and arrange an in-person assessment.</li><li><b>Service boundaries:</b> no remote access, no cloud processing, no investigation of another person, and no guarantee that no exposure remains.</li></ul></div></section>
